Error [jet.MissingDynamicEffectBound]: Dynamic call `Shape::area` has no effect bound
  --> tests/ui/crypto_expert_nonce_trait_dispatch_precedence.jet:12:18
    |
 12 |     return shape.area()
    |                  ^^^^
 Why: A trait value can select any implementation at runtime, and the program holds none of this method to bound the call, so an enclosing effect ceiling needs the trait method's declared row or a ceiling in the trait's `#FX(…)` cap
 Fix: Declare an effect row on `Shape::area`, such as `-[]>` for pure dispatch, put an `#FX(…)` ceiling above the trait, or move this dynamic call outside the bounded function
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0743
